    {
      "id": "claim_922c5d0f03bf4c9fb4aa1f0823e5a0cc",
      "statement": "FormDiffBlock visualizes changes between a baseline Form and a newer import at the position level. For each position, it matches old and new Form rows, reads them as ElementType refs and product codes, and proposes one action per change: Swap (old ET → new ET), Update (change ET's code in place if safe), Fork (create a copy for positions that change while others keep the original), or New ElementType (create a fresh ET for a new code). Click buttons to apply actions; each is one undo step.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/components/FormDiffBlock.jsx#L14-L43",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:216c0346427235f3e84c217b03df8e42e06c61012820831ebf2d176783033839:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/components/FormDiffBlock.jsx#L44-L107",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:be7f37240a9c33dd1cc69f992e9dfd681652bace77099689e2a401d4d615a25e:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_c08ce7179b314bca9972702087095808",
      "statement": "formImpact() interprets Form changes as recipe actions by reading Form rows as codes (known ElementTypes or unknown code-shaped words) and comparing against the recipe's current ElementTypes. It records what changed in the Form, what ElementType(s) are affected, and whether changing one affects others (sharing analysis). If an ET is shared by multiple positions and only some change in the Form, it recommends Fork instead of Update in place.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/utils/formImpact.js#L1-L66",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:c3d94a9fc60bef76633dd0153085889b48fa00cb267a54812371d87ebcb438a0:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_7a29a4a7035e460397585a92ad057150",
      "statement": "formDiff.matchForms() pairs old and new Form rows by position ref and similarity. Rows with identical text under the same ref are marked unchanged (or changed if the manufacturer differs). Unmatched rows are sorted by word-level similarity to find the best pair, else matched in order. Rows nobody pairs with are marked removed.",
